In our approach, we have incorporated new, more accurate predictions derived from the relativistic mean field theory using the Lagrangian density formalism to improve the overall simulation results and match the available experimental constraints. This method utilizes theory-based predictions to enhance our understanding and provide a comprehensive analysis framework for similar future studies involving relativistic heavy ion experiments.
Our simulations successfully match key experimental data from the ${}^{40}$He+ ${}^{40}$He collisions, including fluctuations and spectral flow characteristics. This comparison validates our model as a critical control experiment before utilizing it in more complex systems like those found in the LHC or TN-87$${\rm F}
